{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact MCP Draft6 fc23cdd913bc825e6ca26ea4fa40e55466a956fc, tree916ed0518f681b6108c4f349db4427e0f0414428. Keep Hugh's user-facing names and the complete dynamic service; the new mapping needs these corrections:\n\n1. P2 — Make aliases unique across the entire advertised catalog (plan031:151–172,191–204). The old variant rule groups by the same native definition name and ActType digest; the new rule only prevents two kinds of one definition mapping to one name. Platform register.found→room.create can collide with an unfamiliar room definition's non-genesis create, and directory.open-issue→issue.create with a custom issue.create. A duplicate tool name can hide a valid activity or dispatch ambiguously. Resolve collisions AFTER mapping across all native definitions/kinds. Give deterministic variants based on the full native dispatch/binding identity, not ActType bytes alone: identical ActType objects under different native kind keys can have identical declaration digests while requiring different native routing. Keep unsuffixed names when globally unique, full descriptor binding and refusal before signing on genuine mismatch. W2 must cover mapped platform/custom collisions with differing and byte-identical rows, stable ordering/reconnect, and both activities reachable in every launch mode. Do not reject a valid unfamiliar application to protect a preferred alias.\n\n2. P2/P3 — Separate surface vocabulary from actual native symbols. The Record table at210 says register create, but the exact native register declares genesis install at82 and the ordinary found act at141. Generic surface create dispatches the native genesis; surface room.create must bind register.found, not invent literal native create. The native field-type explanation at384 changes scope to inspect, although inspect is a tool and scope is the contract type. The construction claim at101 calls the existing CLI commands actions/record, while native line.ts61,89,91